        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A line laser is the right tool for almost every job inside a house, and a rotary laser is the right tool for grading, foundations and long outdoor runs. The difference comes down to how you read the beam: by eye on a nearby wall, or with a detector across a site.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most people the best move is a good green cross-line or three-plane laser for everyday work, plus a rented rotary kit for the occasional big outdoor job. Our <a href="/best-laser-level/">laser level buying guide</a> covers both categories.
          </p>
